column1:
1:7|Your country is desolate;
your cities have burned.
Foreigners devour your land before your eyes;
it is desolate, overthrown by strangers.|Keep devastation and witnessed consumption.

2:19|People will enter caves in the rocks
and holes in the earth,
from the terror of the **LORD**,
from the splendor of his majesty,
when he rises to make the earth tremble.|Keep expanded hiding refrain and earth terror.

2:21|to enter clefts in the rocks
and cracks in the cliffs,
from the terror of the **LORD**,
from the splendor of his majesty,
when he rises to make the earth tremble.|Preserve repeated refrain and rock variations.

3:24|Instead of perfume, rot;
instead of a sash, a rope;
instead of styled hair, baldness;
instead of a fine robe, sackcloth;
branding instead of beauty.|Keep five humiliating exchanges.

5:25|So the **LORD**’s anger burned against his people.
He stretched out his hand and struck them;
mountains shook,
and their corpses lay like refuse in the streets.
For all this, his anger has not turned away;
his hand is still stretched out.|Preserve bodies and recurring anger refrain.

5:27|None grows tired or stumbles;
none dozes or sleeps.
No belt at the waist comes loose;
no sandal strap breaks.|Retain four readiness negatives.

9:17|Therefore the Lord takes no pleasure in their young men
and has no compassion on their fatherless or widows,
for everyone is godless and does evil;
every mouth speaks folly.
For all this, his anger has not turned away;
his hand is still stretched out.|Preserve disturbing withheld compassion and exact refrain.

9:21|Manasseh devours Ephraim, and Ephraim Manasseh;
together they turn against Judah.
For all this, his anger has not turned away;
his hand is still stretched out.|Keep intra-Israel conflict and repeated refrain.

15:4|Heshbon and Elealeh cry out;
their voices are heard as far as Jahaz.
So Moab’s armed men cry aloud;
its very life trembles.|Retain soldiers’ grief and three towns.

21:15|They have fled from swords,
from the drawn sword,
from the bent bow,
from the weight of war.|Retain fourfold flight causes.
